/* book Worked example: Q: A coil of resistance 8 Ω and inductance 0.02 H is in series with a 100 µF capacitor across a 230 V, 50 Hz supply. Find the total impedance, the current, and the voltage across the coil.
   1. ω = 2πf = 2π × 50 = 314.16 rad/s.
   2. XL = ωL = 314.16 × 0.02 = 6.28 Ω.
   3. XC = 1/(ωC) = 1/(314.16 × 100 × 10⁻⁶) = 31.83 Ω.
   4. X = XL − XC = 6.28 − 31.83 = −25.55 Ω (capacitive overall).
   5. Z = R + jX = 8 − j25.55 Ω.
   6. |Z| = √(8² + 25.55²) = √(64 + 652.8) = 26.77 Ω.
   7. θ = tan⁻¹(−25.55/8) = −72.6°, so the current leads the supply voltage by 72.6°.
   8. I = V/|Z| = 230/26.77 = 8.59 A.
   9. Coil alone: Zcoil = 8 + j6.28 Ω, |Zcoil| = √(64 + 39.4) = 10.17 Ω.
   10. Vcoil = I × |Zcoil| = 8.59 × 10.17 = 87.4 V.
   Answer: Z = 8 − j25.55 Ω (26.77 Ω at −72.6°), I = 8.59 A leading, and Vcoil = 87.4 V. */
